coder › Fixed `slugify('Crème Brûlée')` → `'creme-brulee'` on branch `fix/slugify-accents` (commit `4293a98`).

What changed:
- `src/slugify.ts`: added `.normalize('NFD')` + `.replace(/[\u0300-\u036f]/g, '')` before lowercasing, so accented Latin letters decompose and their combining marks are dropped to the base letter. Kept the existing `/[^a-z0-9]+/g → '-'` collapse and `/^-+|-+$/g` trim, so empty/punctuation-only input returns `''`.
- `src/slugify.test.ts`: kept the existing `Hello World` test; added tests for accents, dash collapsing, leading/trailing dash trim, empty string, and punctuation-only string.

